            <ArticleTitle>Idiopathic ovarian vein thrombosis: a rare cause of pelvic pain - case report and review of literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>299-301</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1479-828X.2010.01159.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ovarian vein thrombosis is a condition most commonly identified in the puerperium and in association with malignancy, pelvic infections, surgery and thrombophilia. We report a case of idiopathic ovarian vein thrombosis and therefore highlight the importance of considering the diagnosis in women presenting with lower abdominal pain, in whom more common diagnoses cannot be identified.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
